+## Second admitted attempt and Windows header correction
+
+The single v3 attempt on 2026-10-12 at 06:15:26 UTC used source `5a891be` and Plan
+SHA256 `ee6c031d67a028dff0c058e06c6a67b5c0de9c8ef72fc4be8f73de1b533e38e9`.
+Original-handle identity and CIM registration succeeded on the first attempt.
+Local zlib initialization and CMake configuration succeeded. MSBuild emitted the
+zlib/GSC static libraries and the reader-test executable, then failed compiling
+`audit/main.cpp`; no CTest, native negative tests or Beacon binder was run.
+The first error was C2146 at `zconf.h:402` before `Bytef`, followed by C2371 on
+`far`. An unqualified descendant remained two seconds after root exit; the
+original job was stopped, zero active members were confirmed and the lease was
+released. Main's process identity was unchanged; no game files were staged.
+
+The preserved ignored root is `build/native-registration-fixed-20261012`:
+
+- `supervision.json`: `2b25b721be9e56f524d9fefa510d5ddf4d71c54e33f4abcc1ae993fe93a2fcb3`
+- `build-receipt.json`: `f8a8222fb2873a308ddf4ea207485850ee995ab82fafeee8e6579e1652685d6d`
+- `build.stdout.log`: `31f295b64b63bfe1d87b97982ceda986a4b87e79433d0099e8d9c38dd2ab3d4e`
+
+The inspected Windows SDK 10.0.26100.0 `minwindef.h` defines `far` as empty (line
+94) and `FAR` as `far` (line 150). The original include order was Windows/BCrypt,
+xsk IW7, then zlib. IW7 includes `xsk/stdinc.hpp`, which deliberately undefines
+`far` under `_WINDOWS_` (line 40), while `FAR` still expands to the now-undefined
+identifier. zlib therefore parses `typedef Byte far Bytef` at line 402. This
+matches the first compiler error without changing any disassembler behavior.
+
+The correction includes zlib before the xsk IW7 header. Windows/zlib declarations
+are parsed while their macro chain is intact; xsk still removes `far` before its
+own script-engine declarations. Third-party headers, CMake settings and decoder
+logic remain unchanged. A fresh native compile is required to verify the fix.
+
+The actual recorded compiler was MSVC 14.44.35207 Hostx64/x64, SHA256
+`fe251ef50a1545b1b0835ee17b1e785459712b38d79e45b5c1d3d28970a36619`.
+The failed target's `CL.command.1.tlog` contains only its two-byte BOM, so an exact
+expanded `cl.exe` command was not captured and is not reconstructed as evidence.
+The retained generated Release project specifies C++20, MaxSpeed, MultiThreaded
+runtime, `PrecompiledHeader=NotUsing`, no forced include, and definitions `WIN32`,
+`_WINDOWS`, `NDEBUG`, `_WIN32_WINNT=0x0A00`, `CMAKE_INTDIR="Release"`. Include paths
+are the run identity directory, tool include directory and pinned zlib directory.
+MSBuild used the recorded `--parallel 1 -- /m:1 /nr:false
+/p:MultiProcessorCompilation=false` command. Source, dependency, input and compiler
+hashes were unchanged after closure; source occupied 91,980,138 bytes excluding
+build output and run output was about 35.1 MB. The v3 failure remains immutable.
+
 ```text
 python -B audit/prepare.py --output build/identity-reviewed
 cmake -S audit -B build/audit-native -G "Visual Studio 17 2022" -A x64 -DAUDIT_IDENTITY_DIR=ABSOLUTE_IDENTITY_DIRECTORY
